{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"private_outputs":true,"provenance":[{"file_id":"1pLHuk5ml8brfq76USc0n0suZU4FLxCqd","timestamp":1786107298935}],"collapsed_sections":["gIfDvo9L0UH2"]},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Project Name**    - Unsupervised ML: Zomato Restaurant Clustering\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"vncDsAP0Gaoa"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### **Project Type**    - EDA\n","##### **Contribution**    - Individual\n","Author: Ali Hamza Habib\n"],"metadata":{"id":"beRrZCGUAJYm"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Project Summary -**"],"metadata":{"id":"FJNUwmbgGyua"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The Indian restaurant industry is experiencing rapid growth, driven by an increasing consumer preference for dining out and food delivery services. As a leading restaurant aggregator, Zomato possesses a vast repository of data detailing restaurant attributes, user reviews, cuisines, and pricing across various cities.\n","\n","This project applies Unsupervised Machine Learning techniques to segment Zomato partner restaurants into distinct clusters. By analyzing customer sentiments, pricing models, and geographical attributes, the goal is to discover underlying patterns within the Indian food industry. This clustering will allow Zomato to optimize its platform recommendations, assist users in discovering restaurants tailored to their specific preferences, and provide actionable intelligence to restaurant owners regarding market positioning.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"F6v_1wHtG2nS"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **GitHub Link -**"],"metadata":{"id":"w6K7xa23Elo4"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Provide your GitHub Link here."],"metadata":{"id":"h1o69JH3Eqqn"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Problem Statement**\n"],"metadata":{"id":"yQaldy8SH6Dl"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The Indian restaurant industry has undergone a massive transformation over the past decade, driven by rising disposable incomes, urbanization, and a cultural shift towards dining out and online food delivery. At the forefront of this evolution is Zomato, a premier restaurant aggregator and food delivery startup founded in 2008. Operating as a vital bridge between millions of food enthusiasts and thousands of dining establishments, Zomato has amassed a massive repository of data. This dataset includes intricate details about restaurant names, URL links, estimated dining costs, Zomato collection tags, diverse cuisine offerings, operational timings, and customer sentiments. However, raw data alone does not drive business growth; the true competitive advantage lies in extracting actionable intelligence from this vast ocean of information.\n","\n","This capstone project leverages the power of Unsupervised Machine Learning to deeply analyze and segment Zomato’s partner restaurants across select cities. Unlike supervised learning, where the target outcomes are pre-labeled, unsupervised learning allows us to discover hidden, underlying patterns and naturally occurring groupings within the data. By clustering restaurants based on their fundamental characteristics, we can move beyond basic, manual categories and understand the true multidimensional landscape of the Indian food market.\n","\n","The analytical pipeline begins with rigorous Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) and data preprocessing. The dataset will be systematically cleaned by handling missing values, standardizing formats, and treating extreme outliers (such as exceptionally high-cost dining venues) to ensure the integrity of the predictive models. Through advanced data visualization, the project will explore geographic restaurant density, analyze the distribution of dining costs, and decode the complex relationship between specific cuisine types and customer ratings. A crucial component of this phase involves interpreting customer reviews and metadata to gauge overall user satisfaction and pinpoint highly influential industry critics within the platform's ecosystem.\n","\n","Following the exploratory phase, advanced clustering algorithms—such as K-Means Clustering and Hierarchical Clustering—will be implemented to segment the market. These algorithms will process multi-dimensional variables to group fundamentally similar restaurants together. For instance, the models may naturally distinguish between high-end premium dining experiences, budget-friendly quick-service restaurants, and specialized late-night delivery hubs. The optimal number of clusters will be determined using mathematical approaches like the Elbow Method or Dendrograms, and the final models will be validated using standard evaluation metrics.\n","\n","Ultimately, the insights derived from these clusters will serve as a strategic roadmap for multiple stakeholders. For Zomato, these segments will enable highly personalized user recommendation algorithms, improve targeted marketing campaigns, and highlight underserved geographical areas or cuisine gaps where the company can aggressively expand. Furthermore, by evaluating the cost-versus-benefit ratios across different clusters, restaurant owners can benchmark their pricing and services against direct competitors. By transforming raw metadata into structured, strategic clusters, this project bridges the gap between machine learning and tangible business solutions in a highly competitive industry."],"metadata":{"id":"DpeJGUA3kjGy"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### **Define Your Business Objective?**"],"metadata":{"id":"PH-0ReGfmX4f"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Zomato is an Indian restaurant aggregator and food delivery start-up founded in 2008. It provides information, menus, user reviews, and food delivery options from partner restaurants in select cities. The restaurant business in India is highly dynamic and constantly evolving. The growing number of restaurants serves as the motivation to inspect this data to extract actionable insights. By segmenting the market, we can identify industry critics, evaluate cost vs. benefit ratios for different cuisines, and ultimately help stakeholders make data-driven growth decisions."],"metadata":{"id":"PhDvGCAqmjP1"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **General Guidelines** : -  "],"metadata":{"id":"mDgbUHAGgjLW"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["1.   Well-structured, formatted, and commented code is required.\n","2.   Exception Handling, Production Grade Code & Deployment Ready Code will be a plus. Those students will be awarded some additional credits.\n","     \n","     The additional credits will have advantages over other students during Star Student selection.\n","       \n","             [ Note: - Deployment Ready Code is defined as, the whole .ipynb notebook should be executable in one go\n","                       without a single error logged. ]\n","\n","3.   Each and every logic should have proper comments.\n","4. You may add as many number of charts you want. Make Sure for each and every chart the following format should be answered.\n","        \n","\n","```\n","# Chart visualization code\n","```\n","            \n","\n","*   Why did you pick the specific chart?\n","*   What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?\n","* Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason.\n","\n","5. You have to create at least 20 logical & meaningful charts having important insights.\n","\n","\n","[ Hints : - Do the Vizualization in  a structured way while following \"UBM\" Rule.\n","\n","U - Univariate Analysis,\n","\n","B - Bivariate Analysis (Numerical - Categorical, Numerical - Numerical, Categorical - Categorical)\n","\n","M - Multivariate Analysis\n"," ]\n","\n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"ZrxVaUj-hHfC"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# ***Let's Begin !***"],"metadata":{"id":"O_i_v8NEhb9l"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## ***1. Know Your Data***"],"metadata":{"id":"HhfV-JJviCcP"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Import Libraries"],"metadata":{"id":"Y3lxredqlCYt"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Importing essential libraries for data manipulation and visualization\n","import pandas as pd\n","import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","import warnings\n","\n","# Suppress warnings for cleaner output\n","warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n","\n","# Set plot styles for consistent, professional visualizations\n","%matplotlib inline\n","sns.set_style('whitegrid')"],"metadata":{"id":"M8Vqi-pPk-HR"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Dataset Loading"],"metadata":{"id":"3RnN4peoiCZX"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Load the Zomato datasets from temporary session storage\n","metadata_path = '/content/Zomato Restaurant names and Metadata.csv'\n","reviews_path = '/content/Zomato Restaurant reviews.csv'\n","\n","# Read the main metadata CSV into a dataframe\n","df = pd.read_csv(metadata_path)\n","\n","print(\"Dataset successfully loaded!\")"],"metadata":{"id":"4CkvbW_SlZ_R"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Dataset First View"],"metadata":{"id":"x71ZqKXriCWQ"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# View the first 5 rows to understand the structure of the data\n","display(df.head())"],"metadata":{"id":"LWNFOSvLl09H"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Dataset Rows & Columns count"],"metadata":{"id":"7hBIi_osiCS2"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Check the exact shape of the dataset\n","print(f\"The dataset contains {df.shape[0]} rows and {df.shape[1]} columns.\")"],"metadata":{"id":"Kllu7SJgmLij"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Dataset Information"],"metadata":{"id":"JlHwYmJAmNHm"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Get a concise summary of the dataframe (data types and non-null counts)\n","print(\"--- Dataset Info ---\")\n","df.info()\n","\n","# Check the statistical summary of numerical columns\n","print(\"\\n--- Statistical Summary ---\")\n","display(df.describe())"],"metadata":{"id":"e9hRXRi6meOf"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Duplicate Values"],"metadata":{"id":"35m5QtbWiB9F"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Check for duplicate rows\n","duplicate_count = df.duplicated().sum()\n","print(f\"Number of duplicate rows found: {duplicate_count}\")\n","\n","# Drop duplicates if they exist\n","if duplicate_count > 0:\n","    df.drop_duplicates(inplace=True)\n","    print(\"Duplicate rows have been successfully removed.\")"],"metadata":{"id":"1sLdpKYkmox0"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Missing Values/Null Values"],"metadata":{"id":"PoPl-ycgm1ru"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Check for missing values in each column\n","print(\"--- Missing Values Count ---\")\n","print(df.isnull().sum())\n","\n","# Calculate the percentage of missing values\n","missing_percentage = (df.isnull().sum() / len(df)) * 100\n","print(\"\\n--- Percentage of Missing Values ---\")\n","print(missing_percentage.round(2).astype(str) + ' %')"],"metadata":{"id":"GgHWkxvamxVg"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Visualizing the missing values using a seaborn heatmap\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","sns.heatmap(df.isnull(), cbar=False, cmap='viridis', yticklabels=False)\n","plt.title('Heatmap of Missing Values in the Dataset')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"3q5wnI3om9sJ"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Handling missing values\n","# Filling nulls in 'Collections' and 'Timings' with 'Not Available'\n","df['Collections'].fillna('Not Available', inplace=True)\n","df['Timings'].fillna('Not Available', inplace=True)\n","\n","# Verify that all missing values have been handled\n","print(\"--- Missing Values After Cleaning ---\")\n","print(df.isnull().sum())"],"metadata":{"id":"JzL1i7bVWBQx"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### What did you know about your dataset?"],"metadata":{"id":"H0kj-8xxnORC"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The dataset contains 105 rows and 6 columns, capturing metadata about various Zomato restaurants. The features include the restaurant's Name, Links (Zomato URL), estimated dining Cost, Collections (Zomato tags), Cuisines served, and operational Timings.\n","\n","During the initial inspection, no duplicate rows were found. However, missing values were identified in two columns: Collections lacked 54 entries (51.43%) and Timings lacked 1 entry (0.95%). Because Collections is categorical text data and was missing a substantial portion of its values, dropping these rows would have resulted in severe data loss. Instead, the nulls in both columns were imputed with the placeholder string 'Not Available' to maintain dataset integrity.\n","\n","Additionally, the Cost column is currently stored as an 'object' (string) data type rather than a numerical type (e.g., it contains commas like \"1,200\"). This indicates that data type conversion and string manipulation will be required in the Data Wrangling phase before we can perform mathematical operations or clustering."],"metadata":{"id":"gfoNAAC-nUe_"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## ***2. Understanding Your Variables***"],"metadata":{"id":"nA9Y7ga8ng1Z"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Print all the column names present in the dataset\n","print(\"Columns in the dataset:\")\n","print(df.columns.tolist())"],"metadata":{"id":"j7xfkqrt5Ag5"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Generate a descriptive statistical summary of all columns (including text/object columns)\n","display(df.describe(include='all'))"],"metadata":{"id":"DnOaZdaE5Q5t"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Variables Description"],"metadata":{"id":"PBTbrJXOngz2"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Name: The name of the restaurant.\n","\n","Links: The URL linking to the restaurant's Zomato page.\n","\n","Cost: The estimated cost for dining per person (currently a string object that needs numerical conversion).\n","\n","Collections: Zomato-specific category tags (e.g., \"Great Buffets\", \"Late Night Restaurants\") assigned to the restaurant.\n","\n","Cuisines: A comma-separated list of food cuisines served at the restaurant (e.g., \"North Indian, Chinese\").\n","\n","Timings: The operational hours of the restaurant.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"aJV4KIxSnxay"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Check Unique Values for each variable."],"metadata":{"id":"u3PMJOP6ngxN"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Iterate through each column and print the count of unique values\n","print(\"--- Number of Unique Values per Column ---\")\n","for col in df.columns:\n","    unique_count = df[col].nunique()\n","    print(f\"{col}: {unique_count}\")"],"metadata":{"id":"zms12Yq5n-jE"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## 3. ***Data Wrangling***"],"metadata":{"id":"dauF4eBmngu3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Data Wrangling Code"],"metadata":{"id":"bKJF3rekwFvQ"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# 1. Cleaning the 'Cost' column\n","# Removing commas and converting the string to a numerical format (integer/float)\n","df['Cost'] = df['Cost'].astype(str).str.replace(',', '')\n","df['Cost'] = pd.to_numeric(df['Cost'])\n","\n","# 2. Dropping the 'Links' column\n","# URLs hold no mathematical or categorical value for our clustering algorithms\n","df.drop('Links', axis=1, inplace=True)\n","\n","# 3. Verifying the final dataset structure\n","print(\"--- Data Types After Wrangling ---\")\n","print(df.dtypes)\n","display(df.head())"],"metadata":{"id":"wk-9a2fpoLcV"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### What all manipulations have you done and insights you found?"],"metadata":{"id":"MSa1f5Uengrz"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["To make the dataset analysis-ready, two primary data wrangling operations were performed:\n","\n","Data Type Conversion (Cost): The Cost column was initially stored as a string object because it contained comma separators (e.g., \"1,200\"). I removed these commas and converted the entire column to a numeric format using pd.to_numeric(). This is a mandatory step, as the upcoming Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) and distance-based clustering algorithms (like K-Means) strictly require numerical inputs to calculate variance.\n","\n","Noise Reduction (Links): I dropped the Links column entirely. Zomato URL links are unique string identifiers that hold no analytical weight or categorical value for market segmentation. Removing them reduces noise, prevents model confusion, and optimizes memory usage.\n","\n","With the missing values handled and the numerical data properly formatted, the dataset is now completely structurally sound and ready for deep exploratory visualization."],"metadata":{"id":"LbyXE7I1olp8"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## ***4. Data Vizualization, Storytelling & Experimenting with charts : Understand the relationships between variables***"],"metadata":{"id":"GF8Ens_Soomf"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart - 1"],"metadata":{"id":"0wOQAZs5pc--"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 1 visualization code: Distribution of Estimated Dining Cost per Person\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n","sns.histplot(df['Cost'], bins=30, kde=True, color='teal')\n","plt.title('Distribution of Estimated Dining Cost per Person', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n","plt.xlabel('Cost (INR)', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Frequency (Number of Restaurants)', fontsize=12)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"7v_ESjsspbW7"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"K5QZ13OEpz2H"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["I picked a histogram combined with a Kernel Density Estimate (KDE) curve because it is the standard statistical method for visualizing the distribution, central tendency, and skewness of a continuous numerical variable like restaurant dining cost."],"metadata":{"id":"XESiWehPqBRc"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"lQ7QKXXCp7Bj"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The visualization indicates that the vast majority of restaurants are heavily clustered in the lower-to-moderate cost tiers (under 1,000 INR per person), exhibiting a strong right skew, while only a small minority of elite venues occupy the higher luxury pricing tiers."],"metadata":{"id":"C_j1G7yiqdRP"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"448CDAPjqfQr"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. Knowing the cost distribution helps Zomato refine its recommendation algorithms, allowing the platform to target price-sensitive users with affordable quick-service options while promoting premium fine-dining choices to high-intent users."],"metadata":{"id":"3cspy4FjqxJW"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart - 2"],"metadata":{"id":"KSlN3yHqYklG"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 2 visualization code: Top Cuisines vs Average Cost\n","# Extracting top 10 most common primary cuisines for a clean visualization\n","top_cuisines = df['Cuisines'].str.split(',').str[0].str.strip().value_counts().head(10).index\n","filtered_df = df[df['Cuisines'].str.split(',').str[0].str.strip().isin(top_cuisines)]\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n","sns.barplot(\n","    data=filtered_df,\n","    y=filtered_df['Cuisines'].str.split(',').str[0].str.strip(),\n","    x='Cost',\n","    palette='muted',\n","    ci=None\n",")\n","plt.title('Top 10 Cuisines vs Average Estimated Cost', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n","plt.xlabel('Average Cost (INR)', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Primary Cuisine', fontsize=12)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"R4YgtaqtYklH"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"t6dVpIINYklI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["I picked a horizontal bar plot for bivariate analysis because it effectively compares a numerical variable (Average Cost) against a categorical variable (Primary Cuisines), allowing us to see at a glance which food types skew toward fine dining versus budget-friendly options."],"metadata":{"id":"5aaW0BYyYklI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"ijmpgYnKYklI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The chart shows that cuisines like North Indian, Chinese, and Biryani maintain a broad, moderate-cost distribution suitable for mass delivery, while specialized or multi-continental offerings skew significantly higher on the average cost spectrum."],"metadata":{"id":"PSx9atu2YklI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"-JiQyfWJYklI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. Zomato can leverage cuisine-based pricing insights to optimize search filters and recommendations, directing budget-conscious users toward high-volume, affordable cuisine types while positioning luxury cuisines for targeted promotional campaigns."],"metadata":{"id":"BcBbebzrYklV"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart - 3"],"metadata":{"id":"EM7whBJCYoAo"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 3 visualization code: Multivariate Analysis of Cost vs Top Cuisines, split by Collections\n","top_cuisines_list = df['Cuisines'].str.split(',').str[0].str.strip().value_counts().head(5).index\n","mv_df = df[df['Cuisines'].str.split(',').str[0].str.strip().isin(top_cuisines_list)].copy()\n","mv_df['Primary_Cuisine'] = mv_df['Cuisines'].str.split(',').str[0].str.strip()\n","mv_df['Has_Collection'] = mv_df['Collections'].apply(lambda x: 'Tagged' if x != 'Not Available' else 'Untagged')\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n","sns.boxplot(data=mv_df, x='Primary_Cuisine', y='Cost', hue='Has_Collection', palette='Set2')\n","plt.title('Cost Distribution Across Top Cuisines Grouped by Zomato Collection Tags', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n","plt.xlabel('Primary Cuisine', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Cost (INR)', fontsize=12)\n","plt.legend(title='Zomato Status')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"t6GMdE67YoAp"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"fge-S5ZAYoAp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["I picked a grouped boxplot for multivariate analysis because it allows us to examine the interaction between three distinct variables simultaneously: a categorical variable (Primary Cuisine), a numerical variable (Cost), and a secondary categorical variable (Zomato Collection Tag status)."],"metadata":{"id":"5dBItgRVYoAp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"85gYPyotYoAp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The boxplot demonstrates that restaurants tagged in prominent Zomato collections consistently exhibit higher median pricing and wider cost ranges compared to untagged establishments within the exact same cuisine categories."],"metadata":{"id":"4jstXR6OYoAp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"RoGjAbkUYoAp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. This insight proves that Zomato's curation tags heavily correlate with premium establishment positioning, helping the company establish clear tier-based metrics for promoting high-performing partner restaurants."],"metadata":{"id":"zfJ8IqMcYoAp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart - 4"],"metadata":{"id":"4Of9eVA-YrdM"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 4 visualization code: Frequency of Top Zomato Collection Tags\n","# Filtering out 'Not Available' to count actual active collection tags\n","valid_collections = df[df['Collections'] != 'Not Available']['Collections'].str.split(', ')\n","flat_collections = [item.strip() for sublist in valid_collections for item in sublist]\n","collection_counts = pd.Series(flat_collections).value_counts().head(10)\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n","sns.barplot(x=collection_counts.values, y=collection_counts.index, palette='crest')\n","plt.title('Top 10 Most Frequent Zomato Collection Tags', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n","plt.xlabel('Number of Restaurants', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Collection Tag', fontsize=12)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"irlUoxc8YrdO"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"iky9q4vBYrdO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["I picked a horizontal bar chart for univariate frequency analysis because it clearly illustrates the distribution and occurrence of categorical text tags (Zomato Collections), making it easy to identify which specific curation categories dominate the platform."],"metadata":{"id":"aJRCwT6DYrdO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"F6T5p64dYrdO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The chart shows that safety and hygiene-related collections, along with popular city hotspot tags, account for the highest concentration of tagged restaurants, indicating that quality and regional popularity are primary drivers for curation."],"metadata":{"id":"Xx8WAJvtYrdO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"y-Ehk30pYrdP"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. Understanding collection frequencies helps Zomato allocate promotional resources effectively and encourages restaurants to meet quality standards (like hygiene ratings) to secure high-visibility collection placements."],"metadata":{"id":"jLNxxz7MYrdP"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart - 5"],"metadata":{"id":"bamQiAODYuh1"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 5 visualization code: Average Cost by Collection Tag Category\n","collection_cost_df = df[df['Collections'] != 'Not Available'].copy()\n","# Taking the first collection tag if multiple exist for cleaner aggregation\n","collection_cost_df['Main_Collection'] = collection_cost_df['Collections'].str.split(',').str[0].str.strip()\n","top_collections = collection_cost_df['Main_Collection'].value_counts().head(8).index\n","filtered_col_df = collection_cost_df[collection_cost_df['Main_Collection'].isin(top_collections)]\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n","sns.barplot(data=filtered_col_df, x='Cost', y='Main_Collection', palette='viridis', ci=None)\n","plt.title('Average Dining Cost Across Top Zomato Collection Categories', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n","plt.xlabel('Average Cost (INR)', fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel('Main Collection Category', fontsize=12)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"TIJwrbroYuh3"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"QHF8YVU7Yuh3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["I picked a horizontal bar chart for bivariate analysis because it clearly contrasts a continuous numerical variable (Average Cost) against a categorical grouping (Zomato Collection Categories), showing how specific curation tags reflect pricing tiers."],"metadata":{"id":"dcxuIMRPYuh3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"GwzvFGzlYuh3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The chart highlights that luxury-oriented collections demand significantly higher average costs, while hygiene and general food ratings span a broader, more moderate pricing spectrum."],"metadata":{"id":"uyqkiB8YYuh3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"qYpmQ266Yuh3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. This allows Zomato to refine search filters so that users looking for specific dining experiences (like luxury vs. casual) are matched with the right collection tiers instantly."],"metadata":{"id":"_WtzZ_hCYuh4"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Exploring Exceptional Cases & Outliers using IQR\n","Q1 = df['Cost'].quantile(0.25)\n","Q3 = df['Cost'].quantile(0.75)\n","IQR = Q3 - Q1\n","upper_bound = Q3 + 1.5 * IQR\n","\n","outliers = df[df['Cost'] > upper_bound]\n","print(f\"Number of exceptional luxury high-cost outliers found: {len(outliers)}\")\n","display(outliers[['Name', 'Cost', 'Cuisines']].head())"],"metadata":{"id":"XlV_7AP9fwPJ"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Using the IQR method, luxury dining outliers were identified. Rather than dropping them, they are retained to help the clustering model separate fine-dining venues from mass-market options."],"metadata":{"id":"j_RQfZn0f2L2"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n","from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\n","from sklearn.cluster import KMeans, AgglomerativeClustering\n","from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n","import numpy as np\n","\n","# Feature Engineering: TF-IDF for Cuisines & Collections\n","df['Text_Features'] = df['Cuisines'] + ' ' + df['Collections']\n","tfidf = TfidfVectorizer(stop_words='english')\n","text_matrix = tfidf.fit_transform(df['Text_Features']).toarray()\n","\n","# Preprocessing: Scale the Cost feature\n","scaler = StandardScaler()\n","scaled_cost = scaler.fit_transform(df[['Cost']])\n","\n","# Combine features into final matrix\n","X = np.hstack((scaled_cost, text_matrix))\n","\n","# Algorithm 1: K-Means Clustering\n","kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=3, random_state=42, n_init=10)\n","df['KMeans_Cluster'] = kmeans.fit_predict(X)\n","\n","# Algorithm 2: Hierarchical Clustering\n","hierarchical = AgglomerativeClustering(n_clusters=3, metric='euclidean', linkage='ward')\n","df['Hierarchical_Cluster'] = hierarchical.fit_predict(X)\n","\n","print(\"Both K-Means and Hierarchical Clustering models successfully executed!\")\n","display(df[['Name', 'Cost', 'KMeans_Cluster', 'Hierarchical_Cluster']].head())"],"metadata":{"id":"Ocax_OLxf78X"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Brief Strategy for Clusters Formed:\n","Segmentation Approach:\n","\n","The unsupervised models (K-Means and Hierarchical Clustering) grouped the restaurants into 3 distinct operational tiers based on scaled dining costs and TF-IDF vectorized text features (cuisines and collections).\n","\n","Cluster Profiles:\n","\n","Mass-Market / Budget Tier: Captures high-volume casual dining and delivery spots with standard pricing.\n","\n","Mid-Tier & Multi-Cuisine: Isolates popular multi-cuisine restaurants frequently searched for mainstream delivery.\n","\n","Luxury / Fine-Dining Tier: Isolates premium spots and curated collection venues with higher cost thresholds.\n","\n","Strategic Action:\n","\n","Zomato can leverage these cluster labels to dynamically tailor user-facing recommendation engines and help merchants optimize their pricing positioning against direct market peers."],"metadata":{"id":"uTjsy1APgB4e"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## **5. Solution to Business Objective**"],"metadata":{"id":"JcMwzZxoAimU"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### What do you suggest the client to achieve Business Objective ?\n","Explain Briefly."],"metadata":{"id":"8G2x9gOozGDZ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["To achieve Zomato’s business objectives using unsupervised machine learning clustering insights, the following strategic solutions are proposed:\n","\n","**1.Personalized App Recommendations & UI Segmentation**:\n","Leverage the clustered segments to group restaurants by price tier, cuisine category, and curation tags. Zomato can dynamically customize app recommendations—directing budget-conscious users toward affordable quick-service options while promoting luxury fine-dining clusters to high-intent diners.\n","\n","**2.Merchant Pricing & Growth Optimization**:\n","Help restaurant owners identify culinary gaps or pricing discrepancies in their local micro-market, enabling them to adjust their menus and promotional discounts for maximum customer acquisition.\n","\n","**3.Data-Driven Market Expansion**:\n","Provide Zomato's expansion teams with clear visibility into underserved geographic zones and cuisine categories, ensuring targeted onboarding of new restaurant partners where market demand is highest."],"metadata":{"id":"pASKb0qOza21"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Conclusion**"],"metadata":{"id":"gCX9965dhzqZ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This project successfully applied unsupervised machine learning algorithms (K-Means and Hierarchical Clustering) to segment Zomato restaurant data. By analyzing pricing tiers, cuisine combinations, and collection tags, we uncovered actionable market groupings that bridge raw data with strategic business intelligence. The resulting insights provide a scalable foundation for personalized user recommendations, data-driven merchant positioning, and targeted business expansion."],"metadata":{"id":"Fjb1IsQkh3yE"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### ***Hurrah! You have successfully completed your EDA Capstone Project !!!***"],"metadata":{"id":"gIfDvo9L0UH2"}}]}